{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/$volume","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/Create-your-first-2D-game-project."]],"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine","modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/Create-your-first-2D-game-project.","projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateProject#Create-project-using-Xcode","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Intro"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-an-app"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Create-a-main-camera"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#First-sprite"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/CreateFirst2DScene#Make-it-move"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Player-component"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/PlayerAndText#Add-Text-component"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Base-of-Event-Subscriber-pattern","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Subscribe-to-scene-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Type-of-events","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners#Additional-for-physics","kind":"task"}]}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UI-and-Input","projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Create-the-app-shell"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Layout-with-stacks","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Add-a-button-and-state","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics#Debug-overlays","kind":"task"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Create-the-view"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Prepare-layout-helpers"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Create-a-custom-TextRenderer"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/AnimatedText#Apply-and-animate"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Set-up-the-world"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Create-the-input-system","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Read-buttons","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/GamepadInput#Move-and-rumble","kind":"task"}]}]}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/EventListeners","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"project","sections":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you will learn about the event listeners system in Ada."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"How can you catch events and process them"}]}],"estimatedTimeInMinutes":5,"kind":"hero","chapter":"Create your first 2D game project.","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.2 or later","title":"Event Listeners in Ada"},{"tasks":[{"anchor":"Base-of-Event-Subscriber-pattern","stepsSection":[],"contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Event listeners in Ada are built on the Observer pattern.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Its main concept is based on the fact that there is a certain Subject that can send any events.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"And there is an Observer that can receive and process this event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In addition, Observer “subscribes” to events, as if you had subscribed to your favorite blog or magazine - as soon as an event occurs, Observer immediately knows about it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"EL-1.jpg","mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"title":"Base of Event-Subscriber pattern"},{"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-1-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s say we have a plugin in which we would like to listen to some events."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-2-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First of all, to control subscription\/unsubscription to events and for proper memory management, we must create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disposeBag"},{"type":"text","text":" using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Local"},{"type":"text","text":" property wrapper."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"We also mark our plugin with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" to ensure thread safety."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After that, in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setup(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method you can call some code to subscribe to the event."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app.main.subscribe"},{"type":"text","text":" method helps with this."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When an event is triggered, our listener subscribes to it and in the callback we can process our event."}]}],"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-3-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null}],"anchor":"Subscribe-to-scene-events","title":"Subscribe to scene events","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Having understood how the Observer pattern works, let’s look at how to subscribe to scene events using the Plugin pattern.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}]},{"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-3-scene.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the previous section, we saw the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SceneEvents.OnReady"},{"type":"text","text":" event."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ada has several available events that you can handle."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can find out what state your current game scene is in."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can add your own additional logic when any built-in event occurs."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-4-events.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here, as an example, are some built-in events that may be useful to you."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Familiar scene events and new collision events."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"anchor":"Type-of-events","title":"Type of events","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What events can we use? Let’s look at a couple of code examples in Ada."}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}]},{"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s continue with the example we looked at earlier.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"We can access our event and assign the necessary parameters to the properties of the physical component.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that we use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @MainActor in ... }"},{"text":" to ensure we’re on the main actor when modifying physics properties.","type":"text"}]}],"caption":[],"type":"step","code":"EL-2-5-physics.swift","runtimePreview":null}],"anchor":"Additional-for-physics","title":"Additional for physics","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additional information for handling physics in a game engine."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"With the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"physicsWorld2D"},{"type":"text","text":" component you can control the physics settings for any objects in our game."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can set the gravity to zero for the scene creation event."}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}]}],"kind":"tasks"},{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a simple UI screen using Ada views. You will create a window, layout a few elements, and add a button with state."}],"kind":"callToAction","action":{"overridingTitle":"Get started","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/tutorials\/AdaEngine\/UIBasics","isActive":true},"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","title":"UI Basics"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/adaengine\/eventlisteners"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"AdaEngine","category":"Ada","role":"project","title":"Event Listene